<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      The editor Activity used to hardcode Theme.Material.Light, so a host running in dark mode
      dropped the user onto a white screen. The platform has no Material DayNight theme, so the
      light and dark variants are declared here.

      MissionGoFeedbackTheme follows the system, through the -night resource qualifier. That is
      not enough on its own: a host with its own in-app light/dark setting (Compose apps
      typically have one) does not change the resource configuration, so a user who picked dark
      inside a light system would still land on a white page. Such a host sets
      MissionGoOptions.editorAppearance and the Activity applies one of the two explicit themes
      below instead.

      Everything the Activity draws before the H5 loads reads its colours from the theme, which
      is what makes the fix complete: switching the theme alone would still leave a light
      loading screen, because those colours were literals in the code.
    -->
    <style name="MissionGoFeedbackTheme" parent="@android:style/Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar" />

    <style name="MissionGoFeedbackTheme.Light" parent="@android:style/Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar" />

    <style name="MissionGoFeedbackTheme.Dark" parent="@android:style/Theme.Material.NoActionBar" />
</resources>
